\import{ftip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\taxon{Definition}
\tag{ftip}
\title{Conceptual transfer and constructive invention}

\p{Fix a task family, an initial artifact, an admissible interaction protocol,
and a charged resource cap. A research trace records how a system moves from
a difficulty to a reusable capability. Its \newvocab{research-capability profile}
is a tuple of separately measured fields, not a scalar intelligence score:}
##{
\mathcal I=(I_{\mathrm{diag}},I_{\mathrm{transfer}},I_{\mathrm{remix}},
I_{\mathrm{construct}},I_{\mathrm{consequence}},I_{\mathrm{verify}},
I_{\mathrm{acquire}}).
}
\p{The fields record, respectively, whether the system can diagnose a failed
approach, move a useful concept across a stated boundary, combine several
concepts, construct a resource that was not supplied, derive consequences,
validate the result independently, and retain the capability after the
research interaction ends. Each field is conditional on the task law,
protocol, evidence standard and resource accounting; it may be unmeasured or
inapplicable. The profile therefore complements the architecture-conditioned
vector in [Capability vector and conditional frontier](ftip-00JM) without
redefining its coordinates.}

\p{A \newvocab{conceptual transfer} begins with a source concept and a target
problem. It identifies the source's usable structure, gives a map or analogy
that preserves the relevant relations, adapts the concept to the target
representation, and supplies a checkable consequence. Merely mentioning a
similar idea is retrieval; applying a relevant idea to a new problem is
\em{associative application}. Transfer is established by the preserved
structure and the target-side result, not by verbal resemblance.}

\p{A \newvocab{remix} composes two or more source concepts whose joint use was
not already supplied as a completed method. The trace must state the interface
between the concepts, the new dependency or composition rule, and the result
that depends essentially on that combination. A longer list of familiar steps
is not a remix when no new relation is needed.}

\p{A \newvocab{constructive invention} responds to a diagnosed obstruction.
The system identifies a precise hole in the current representation or method,
reformulates that hole as a portable difficulty, and constructs an object,
representation, question or governing principle that fills it. A positive
construction argument contains a checkable construction, an essential new
resource, consequences beyond the original target, and an account of why the
resource was not already present in the admitted starting material. This is the
sense of imaginative construction used here; novelty is assessed relative to
the declared endowment and also reported separately from historical novelty.}

\p{These operations have different failure boundaries. A system may diagnose an
obstruction without transferring a concept, transfer a concept without
remixing it, or construct a useful object without proving its consequences.
Proof and independent verification remain separate fields. Acquisition adds a
further condition: after the contributor, search aid or temporary context is
removed, the frozen recipient must use the retained artifact on fresh tasks.
A successful assisted answer alone does not establish retained capability.}

\p{The profile describes an ability under a specified setup. A tool, curriculum,
contributor or persistent archive can facilitate an operation and can also
become part of the retained artifact; the evidence must state which occurred.
The profile is therefore compatible with model learning, external setup and
successive model generations while keeping those causal routes distinct.}

\p{The profile develops the convex-hull discussion of [contribution grades](https://gist.github.com/utensil/8850752d3d611cb8760b0fbaf724f256) by making associative application, transfer, remixing and construction observable as different outcomes. The accompanying [review of discovery mechanisms](https://utensil.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/580957-tasks/topic/math-agents/near/631170619) is an operational audit of these distinctions; it does not determine the capability definitions or establish a performance result.}
